# Test: ze validate config <file> via unified verb dispatch
# VALIDATES: validate config verb dispatches to the validate handler and answers
#            the verdict for the file it read.
# PREVENTS: regression in unified verb dispatch for validate command
#
# The assertion reads the ANSWER, not a sentence. `validate config` is registered
# through registry.MustRegisterLocalData with command.RenderLocalAnswer, so it
# answers a diagnostic.ValidateResult and the pipe layer renders it
# (ai/rules/cli.md). Until 2026-08-30 the same path was a MustRegisterLocalMeta
# forward to `Run(["validate", ...])`, so this file pinned that printer's first
# line, "configuration valid: <path>". Commit f0ce6a8d4b replaced the forward and
# did not update the pin, which is the only reason this test went red: no
# renderer was dropped, and every one of the 18 production MustRegisterLocalData
# registrations passes the same command.RenderLocalAnswer.
#
# `ze config validate <file>` is a DIFFERENT command, the offline printer under
# the `config` root, and it keeps that sentence. test/parse/cli-validate-valid.ci
# asserts it there, as test/parse/cli-config-dump.ci does for the `ze config dump`
# half of the same pair.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_STDIN
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 65533
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_STDIN

tmpfs=test.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	router-id 10.0.0.1
	session {
		asn {
			local 65533
		}
	}
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				remote 65534
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze validate config test.conf
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:pattern=valid\s+true
expect=stdout:pattern=path\s+test\.conf
